  "note": "Metal Slug 3 as the FBNeo core gives it (retro_get_system_av_info: base 304 x 224, aspect 1.333333, 59.18 Hz; game pixels almost square, 0.982). The deck is drawn on a canvas of game pixels and enlarged on the same column and row grid as the game (nearest neighbour). The Deck pixel is the game pixel while the rail holds its plates in full form, half the game pixel otherwise (deckPixel auto), each game pixel cut in 2 x 2 Deck pixels on the same grid."
 },
 "placement": {
  "anchor": "right",
  "railMin": 56,
  "note": "Game pushed to the right at full screen height (no black band above or below), the rail takes the width left on the left; railMin only shrinks the game on a screen too narrow to leave 56 game pixels (the compact rail). 1920 x 1080: game 1440 x 1080, rail 480 px = 101 game pixels. 1920 x 1200: game 1600 x 1200, rail 320 px = 61 game pixels, drawn at half the game pixel (122 Deck pixels): every plate in full form, lives and grenades back."
 },
